working_notes/failed_attempts.md:61:Failed without a limiting argument. A finite-grid prefix gap only lower-bounds learners restricted to that grid. Under strict crossing, a coarse grid may not contain quotes just below thresholds, so even \(v_c=c\) can fail on the grid. To lower-bound the original continuum-action problem, define \(\kappa\) over \([0,1]\) with `sup` conventions or pass through dense grids/\(\eta\)-comparators.
