+**CL-023: Sharp finite-\(m\) multi-threshold constant.**  
+Status: plausible construction; upper bound not yet proved.  
+For the supremum over choices of \(m\) terminal thresholds with top threshold normalized to \(1\), the candidate sharp local gap is
+\[
+\kappa_m^*=\left(\frac{m-1}{m}\right)^m.
+\]
+The construction uses \(r=(m-1)/m\), thresholds \(c_i=r^{m-i}\), and equal-revenue tails \(\Pr(C\ge c_i)=r^{i-1}\). This recovers \(1/4\) at \(m=2\) and approaches \(1/e\). It is false if read as the value for every fixed \(m\)-point threshold set; e.g. \(\{0.9,1\}\) has two-threshold gap \(0.09\). A rigorous upper proof for support size \(m\) is still needed.
